The  driver  supports  the  Intel  PIIX,  PIIX3, PIIX4, and 82801
(ICH/ICH0/ICH2/ICH3/ICH4/ICH5/ICH6/ICH7/ICH8/ICH9/ICH10) IDE/SATA
controllers and provides the interface with the hardware for  the
driver.   The  0x0002  flag  forces  the driver to disable DMA on
chipsets for which DMA would normally be enabled.   This  can  be
used as a debugging aid, or to work around problems where the IDE
controller  is  wired  up to the system incorrectly.  The timings
used for the PIO and DMA modes for controllers listed  above  are
for  a PCI bus running at 30 or 33 MHz.  This driver may not work
properly on overclocked systems.
